+# Hamlib Backend: RGO ONE
+
+**Manufacturer:** LZ2JR
+
+| Model | Model ID | Status | Backend version |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| RGO ONE V6 | 43001 (`RIG_MODEL_RGOONE_V6`) | RIG_STATUS_BETA | 20261007.0 |
+| RGO ONE V1-V5 | 43002 (`RIG_MODEL_RGOONE_V1V5`) | RIG_STATUS_BETA | 20261007.0 |
+
+## Description
+
+### RGO ONE V6 (model 43001)
+
+All-mode HF transceiver (1.8-29.7 MHz, 50W CW/SSB/FM/RTTY, 12.5W AM).
+STM32 microcontroller, USB CDC ACM interface. Extended TS-480SAT-compatible CAT protocol
+with custom commands. This backend builds on the existing Kenwood protocol layer in
+`rigs/kenwood/` and adds custom implementations wherever the RGO ONE V6 deviates from
+TS-480 behaviour.
+
+CAT reference: `RGO_ONE_V6_CAT_Manual1.03.pdf` (located in this directory).
+
+### RGO ONE V1-V5 (model 43002)
+
+Earlier hardware versions of the RGO ONE. Atmel AVR microcontroller, FTDI USB chip.
+Reduced TS-480SAT-compatible CAT protocol. The confirmed working command set (firmware
+2.51a, verified by Don WB8YQJ) covers frequency, mode, VFO, RIT, AGC, keyer speed,
+key lock, band up/down and PTT. The V1-V5 backend is essentially a restricted TS-480
+profile with the confirmed RGO ONE deviations applied.
+
+**Note:** This backend has not been tested against real V1-V5 hardware by the author.
+It is based on the verified command list from Don WB8YQJ (firmware 2.51a, January 2024).
+
+Key differences from V6:
+- `ID;` returns `ID020` (same as TS-480SAT, not `ID006`)
+- Only `TX0;`/`RX;` for PTT — `TX1` and `TX2` not available
+- `RIG_PTT_ON_DATA` mapped to `TX0` (same logic as V6, for WSJT-X / fldigi compatibility)
+- No antenna tuner (AC/TX2), no RF power control (PC), no attenuator (RA), no S-meter (SM)
+- No RIT-down (RD) — only positive RIT offsets can be set; get_rit reads from IF frame
+- No Windows RTS workaround needed (FTDI chip handles RTS correctly)
+
+## Test status (as of 2026-05-17)
+
+Comprehensive hardware testing completed using the automated test script.
+82 of 82 tests passed, including PTT (TX0/TX2), antenna tuner cycle (TX2),
+and the raw CAT command section (AI, FS, PB).
+1 test may be skipped depending on band position (AI1 BD restore, if already
+at the lowest band no change event is triggered).
+
+Real-world operation tested over many days with QLog 0.50.0 (Flatpak),
+WSJT-X, and OpenWebRX via Hamlib NET rigctl — frequency, mode, band changes,
+PTT and split work without issues. Tested exclusively under Linux.
+
+```
+Opened rig model 43001, 'RGO ONE V6'
+Backend version: 20260612.2, Status: Beta
+rgo_one_open: RGO ONE V6 identified: ID006
+```
+
+The full firmware version and serial numbers are returned by `get_info` (`rigctl i`):
+
+```
+RGO ONE V6 ID006 FW1.08 SN:20303656 32435013 005D0069
+```
+
+| Function | Status |
+|---|---|
+| Connection, identification (ID) | Hardware tested |
+| VFO readback (IF) | Hardware tested |
+| Frequency read/set (FA/FB) | Hardware tested |
+| Operating mode (MD) | Hardware tested |
+| PTT (TX/RX) | Hardware tested (optional `--ptt` test) |
+| Antenna tuner (AC) | Hardware tested (optional `--tune` test) |
+| RIT/XIT (RU/RD/RT/XT) | Hardware tested |
+| Levels (RF, AGC, NB, NL, PA, RA, MG, ML, PC, VD, VG, SD, PL) | Hardware tested |
+| Meters (S-meter SM, SWR, ALC, COMP, RF power) | Hardware tested |
+| CW keyer (KY, KS) | Hardware tested |
+| Split VFO (FR/FT) | Hardware tested |
+| Band ops (BD/BU, incl. frequency verification) | Hardware tested |
+| Key lock (LK) | Hardware tested |
+| AI (auto-info), FS (fine tuning), PB (memory playback) | Hardware tested via raw CAT |
