+### IF frame format (TS-480 compatible, 37 bytes)
+
+The `IF;` command returns the full transceiver status. The response is stored in
+`priv->info` in kenwood.c and used internally by virtually all poll-based functions.
+
+| Position | Field | Hamlib use |
+|---|---|---|
+| [0..1] | `"IF"` identifier | Response validation (`kenwood_safe_transaction`) |
+| [2..12] | VFO A frequency, 11 digits (Hz) | `kenwood_get_freq`, `kenwood_get_vfo_if` |
+| [13..16] | Field delimiter (4 spaces) | (separator, not parsed) |
+| [17..22] | RIT/XIT offset incl. sign (6 chars) | `kenwood_get_rit`, `kenwood_get_xit` |
+| [23] | XIT on/off | `kenwood_get_func(XIT)` |
+| [24] | RIT on/off | `kenwood_get_func(RIT)` |
+| [25] | Receive mode indicator | Not used by Hamlib |
+| [26..27] | Memory channel (2 digits) | `kenwood_get_mem` |
+| [28] | TX state: 0=RX, 1=TX | `kenwood_get_ptt` |
+| [29] | Mode: 1=LSB, 2=USB, 3=CW, 4=FM, 5=AM, 6=FSK, 7=CW-R | `kenwood_get_mode` |
+| [30] | VFO function | `kenwood_get_vfo_if`, `kenwood_get_split_vfo_if` |
+| [31] | Scan on/off | Not used by Hamlib |
+| [32] | Split | `kenwood_get_split_vfo_if` |
+| [33] | Tone type | Not used by Hamlib |
+| [34..35] | Tone number (2 digits) | `kenwood_get_ctcss_tone` |
+| [36] | Trailing space | (padding) |
+
+Positions [0]/[1] are used for validation, not counted as "data" fields.
+Positions [25], [31], [33] are received but not evaluated by any Hamlib function.
+
+The `_parse_if_frame()` helper in `test_rgo_one.py` uses positions [2..12] (frequency),
+[28] (TX state), and [29] (mode) to validate AI-mode IF frames during `test_raw_cat`.
+
+### RGO commands NOT implemented
+
+| CAT command | Description | Reason |
+|---|---|---|
+| **AI** | Auto-info: sends IF frame automatically on changes (transceive mode) | Hamlib transceive support is rudimentary and barely used by any logging software. Polling is sufficient for practical operation. Hamlib disables AI on every connect (`AI0;` in `kenwood_open`). **Tested via raw CAT** in `test_raw_cat`: AI2 (periodic IF frames every ~1.5 s) and AI1 (change-notification IF frames after BU/BD) are captured and parsed. |
+| **FS** | Fine tuning (1Hz step on/off) | Purely manual operation; no meaningful use case for CAT control. **Tested via raw CAT** in `test_raw_cat`: read/set/verify/restore cycle using `send_no_response`. |
+| **PB** | Play CW/SSB memory messages (4 channels, PBP1P2) | Hamlib has no standardised API for memory message playback. `send_morse` (KY) is implemented for live CW, but memory playback is not addressed by any logging software via Hamlib. Direct use via `rigctl w "PB11;"` is possible without any backend changes. Could become relevant if Hamlib introduces a memory message API. **Tested read-only via raw CAT** in `test_raw_cat`. |
+
+### Deliberately NOT implemented
+
+| CAT command | Description | Reason |
+|---|---|---|
+| **EX** | Extended menu (000-083): 84 configuration parameters (sidetone, keyer mode, display, scan, ...) | The menu as a whole cannot be meaningfully mapped -- each entry would need to be individually implemented as a Hamlib config token, and logging software does not access these parameters anyway. Individual EX entries can be added as dedicated level or config parameters if needed (e.g. CW pitch via EX). |
+| **UN** | Transceiver unlock (service command) | Relevant only for factory service, no use in normal operation. |
+
+### Kenwood commands in the code, NOT in the RGO reference
+
+These commands are used by delegated Kenwood functions and are not documented in the
+RGO CAT manual. They may or may not work via TS-480 compatibility.
+
+| CAT command | Used for | Risk |
+|---|---|---|
+| **AG0** | AF gain (volume) | Medium -- basic function, likely TS-480-compatible |
+| **SQ0** | Squelch | Medium -- likely TS-480-compatible |
+| **SR** | Reset (VFO/master) | Medium -- `kenwood_reset` delegated |
+
+### Deliberately removed commands (vs. TS-480)
+
+| Function | Reason |
+|---|---|
+| **BY** (DCD/busy) | Not in RGO manual. `dcd_type = RIG_DCD_NONE` set. |
+| **PR** (speech processor on/off) | Not in RGO manual. Use `PL` level instead of FUNC_COMP. |
+| **VX** (VOX on/off) | Not in RGO manual. VOX is disabled via `VG000` (gain=0). |
+| **NR** (noise reduction) | No direct CAT command. NR is optionally fitted; control (on/off + dB attenuation) is via EX menu item 44. Could be implemented as `LVL_NR` / `FUNC_NR` via EX once individual EX entries are added. |
+| **PT** (CW pitch direct) | Not in RGO manual. Would be possible via EX menu. |
+| **UP/DN** (frequency up/down) | Not in RGO manual. Removed from VFO_OPS. |
+| **VV** (VFO copy) | Not in RGO manual. Removed from VFO_OPS. |
+| **CWPITCH** level | No direct command. Would need to be implemented via EX menu. |
