+## Building
+
+```bash
+# Prerequisites (Debian/Ubuntu)
+sudo apt install build-essential automake autoconf libtool pkg-config \
+    libusb-1.0-0-dev libreadline-dev
+
+# In the Hamlib source directory
+autoreconf -fi
+./configure
+make -j$(nproc)
+
+# Check that both RGO ONE models are recognised
+./tests/rigctl -l | grep -i rgo
+# Expected output:
+# 43001  LZ2JR   RGO ONE V6     20260612.2   Beta   RIG_MODEL_RGOONE_V6
+# 43002  LZ2JR   RGO ONE V1-V5  20260603.0   Beta   RIG_MODEL_RGOONE_V1V5
+
+```
+
+## System-wide installation
+
+```bash
+cd hamlib-4.7.1
+./configure --prefix=/usr/local
+make -j$(nproc)
+sudo make install
+sudo ldconfig
+```
+
+Verify afterwards:
+
+```bash
+/usr/local/bin/rigctl --version
+ls /usr/local/lib/libhamlib.so.5*
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+The RGO ONE appears on the USB port as `/dev/ttyACM0` (CDC ACM, no FTDI adapter
+needed). The exact device name may vary -- check with:
+
+```bash
+ls /dev/ttyACM* /dev/ttyUSB*
+```
+
+### rigctl (interactive)
+
+```bash
+/usr/local/bin/rigctl -m 43001 -r /dev/ttyACM0 -s 9600
+
+# Common commands:
+#   f          - read frequency
+#   F 14250000 - set frequency (14.250 MHz)
+#   m          - read operating mode
+#   M USB 2700 - set USB with 2.7 kHz filter
+#   t          - read PTT state
+#   T 1        - PTT on
+#   T 0        - PTT off
+#   G TUNE     - start antenna tuner cycle (TX2, transmits!)
+
+```
+
+For verbose debug output (diagnostics):
+
+```bash
+/usr/local/bin/rigctl -m 43001 -r /dev/ttyACM0 -s 9600 -vvvv f
+```
+
+### rigctld + QLog (Flatpak)
+
+QLog as a Flatpak bundles its own older Hamlib without RGO ONE support.
+The solution: run `rigctld` as a daemon with the new Hamlib -- QLog then
+connects over the network and does not need its own Hamlib for the protocol.
+
+**Tested and confirmed** with QLog 0.50.0 (Flatpak) on 2026-04-27.
+
+**Step 1:** Start rigctld.
+
+In the background (normal operation):
+
+```bash
+/usr/local/bin/rigctld -m 43001 -r /dev/ttyACM0 -s 57600 -t 4532
+```
+
+In the foreground with log output (diagnostics):
+
+```bash
+/usr/local/bin/rigctld -m 43001 -r /dev/ttyACM0 -s 57600 -t 4532 -vvv
+```
+
+Log levels: `-v` warning, `-vv` verbose, `-vvv` debug, `-vvvv` trace (very detailed).
+
+**Step 2:** Configure in QLog under "New device":
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Manufacturer | Hamlib |
+| Model | NET rigctl |
+| Address | 127.0.0.1 |
+| Port | 4532 |
+
+This keeps QLog unchanged while still using the current Hamlib version.
+The same approach works for WSJT-X, fldigi, and other Flatpak applications.
+
+**Note on baud rate:** For the USB port (CDC ACM) the host-side baud rate does not
+matter -- the USB protocol handles communication. Menu item 22 in the RGO ONE applies
+to the TTL UART (DB15 rear connector) only. `-s 57600` is a safe default.
+
+## Serial interface
+
+- **USB:** Virtual COM port (USB driver required)
+- **TTL UART:** DB15 connector on rear panel (pin 4=GND, pin 5=TX, pin 6=RX)
+- **Baud rates:** 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600 (menu item 22 applies to TTL port only)
+- **Format:** 8N1, no handshake
+
